{"name":"Gone Fishing","hex":"#52a8b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gone fishing","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see go,‎ fishing.","Unavailable, having taken time off for recreation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gone_fishing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gone Fishin' (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Gone Fishin' is a 1997 American comedy film starring Joe Pesci and Danny Glover as two bumbling fishing enthusiasts. Nick Brimble, Rosanna Arquette, Lynn Whitfield, and Willie Nelson co-star. It is the only collaboration between Glover and Pesci outside of the Lethal Weapon franchise. Christopher Cain directed the film. J. J. Abrams and Jill Mazursky wrote the film's script."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Gone_fishin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gone_Fishin'_(film)","wikidata":"Q1192024"},{"title":"Gone Fishing (2008 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Gone Fishing is a 2008 short film written and directed by Chris Jones, starring Bill Paterson and James Wilson, that premiered at BAFTA on 12 January 2008."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/31/Gone_Fishing_Short_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gone_Fishing_(2008_film)","wikidata":"Q5581561"},{"title":"Fishing","blocks":[{"text":"Fishing is the activity of trying to catch fish. Fish are often caught as wildlife from the natural environment, but may also be caught from stocked bodies of water such as ponds, canals, park wetlands and reservoirs. Fishing techniques include trawling, longlining, jigging, hand-gathering, spearing, netting, angling, shooting and trapping, as well as more destructive and often illegal techniques such as electrocution, blasting and poisoning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Stilts_fishermen_Sri_Lanka_02.jpg/330px-Stilts_fishermen_Sri_Lanka_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishing","wikidata":"Q14373"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/P%C3%A1tzcuaro-Trad-Fishing-3.jpg/500px-P%C3%A1tzcuaro-Trad-Fishing-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/P%C3%A1tzcuaro-Trad-Fishing-3.jpg/500px-P%C3%A1tzcuaro-Trad-Fishing-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AP%C3%A1tzcuaro-Trad-Fishing-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Fishing_tools_stone_age_SPMZ.jpg/500px-Fishing_tools_stone_age_SPMZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Fishing_tools_stone_age_SPMZ.jpg/500px-Fishing_tools_stone_age_SPMZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fishing tools from the Mesolithic and Neolithic period","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFishing_tools_stone_age_SPMZ.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/A_Brixham_trawler.jpg/500px-A_Brixham_trawler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/A_Brixham_trawler.jpg/500px-A_Brixham_trawler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Painting of A Brixham trawler by William Adolphus Knell. The painting is now in the National Maritime Museum.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Brixham_trawler.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Louis_John_Rhead_-_Izaak_Wa